+## 2026-11-17
+- **Improved:** Gameplay and other no-speech videos now get their best moments from what happens on screen, not just from the loudest sound. The picker watches for several visible changes at once — flashes, banners, on-screen events, sustained movement, screen shake — keeps the build-up before the action and ends after the payoff, and explains each pick. A loud sound with nothing visible happening (like a distant explosion) no longer outranks a real moment. Set `FRAME_EVIDENCE_SELECTION=0` to switch back to the older sound-and-scene-cut picker.
+
 ## 2026-11-16
 - **Fixed:** The hook title and the captions still chose their height clip by clip, so across the clips of one task the title could sit at the top in one clip and lower down in the next, and the captions rode at a different height in every clip. Both heights are now chosen once for the whole task, worked out from every clip's framing together so the shared heights keep text off faces in all of them, and every clip of the task is rendered with those same heights. A clip whose own framing cannot use the shared height places its text the way it did before and notes the difference in its render report. Re-rendering or regenerating a clip reuses the task's saved heights, so its text lands exactly where the original render put it. Tasks created before this change have no saved heights and render exactly as they did. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** Finance and study clips can now use a "mistake-fix" hook title — one that names the mistake the speaker themselves warns about ("Stop spending your whole salary in the first week"), instead of a general problem or curiosity title. The style is strict about honesty: the title is built only from the warning's own words, so it can never name a mistake the speaker did not raise, and it is only used when the clip also delivers the fix in its first third — a clip that raises a mistake but holds the answer back, or delivers it late, keeps the existing title styles instead. It is available for finance and education clips as a candidate style being tested; the title style those clips use by default is unchanged. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
